# What stays out of the npm package. The "files" list in package.json is the
# working rule: it names what goes in, and its "!" lines what inside those
# folders stays out (npm reads neither .gitignore nor this file for what a
# named folder holds). This file mirrors .gitignore all the same, so the
# exclusions are in one plain place and hold if that behaviour ever changes.
.DS_Store
*.log
*.mkv
*.mp4
# the page for recording the seal, a tool, not the product
web/seal.html
# only the fonts live in web/assets: brand marks and screenshots are not part of the code
web/assets/*.png
web/assets/*.svg
# never inside the package whatever folder they turn up in
.dev/
.internal/
CLAUDE.md
user_input/
user_output/
test/snapshots
